<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José de Escandón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1700">1700</a>–<a href="/years/1770">1770</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José de Escandón was a Spanish military officer and colonial administrator commissioned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> in 1746 to colonise the Gulf coast north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampico">Tampico</a>. From 1748 he founded more than twenty towns and missions between the Pánuco and Nueces rivers, creating the province of Nuevo Santander, the later Mexican state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamaulipas">Tamaulipas</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-de-escandon.jpg" alt="José de Escandón" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_de_Escand%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
